2) REAPER syntax (concise grammar summary)
Use indentation for blocks. Indentation-based like Python. Statements are newline-terminated. Comments use #.

program        := statement*
statement      := simple_stmt | compound_stmt
simple_stmt    := expr_stmt | control_stmt | action_stmt
expr_stmt      := IDENTIFIER "=" expression
control_stmt   := "if" expression ":" NEWLINE INDENT block DEDENT
               |  "while" expression ":" NEWLINE INDENT block DEDENT
               |  "for" IDENT "in" expression ":" NEWLINE INDENT block DEDENT
action_stmt    := builtin_call
block          := statement*
expression     := literal | IDENT | call | binary_op | unary_op | access
call           := IDENT "(" arglist? ")"
arglist        := expression ("," expression)*
literal        := number | string | true | false | null
number         := integer | float
access         := IDENT "." IDENT
binary_op      := expression OP expression   # + - * / > < >= <= == != && || (domain ops)
unary_op       := "-" expression | "!" expression
Extras:

@hot, @simd, @no_heap annotations allowed above function or loop definitions.

loop: is a special infinite event-loop shorthand (sugar for while true:).

when block for mempool events: when tx matches <pattern>:.

